  <title>Structural navigation</title>
  <p>
    Structural navigation lets you move among objects by type such as headings, links, buttons
    and other interactive controls, lists, landmarks, tables, and large text blocks.
  </p>
  <p>
    Structural navigation is not limited to web content. It can be used in document content and
    also in application user interfaces. It relies on the accessible collections interface, an
    API that lets Orca search the entire accessibility tree quickly. This tree is the structured
    view of an application's objects provided to assistive technologies. Applications and
    toolkits that do not support this interface, or omit objects from the tree, will not work as
    expected.
  </p>
  <p>
    The large object commands find large text blocks; use Large object length to set their
    minimum size. Internal frames are documents embedded within another page.
  </p>
  <p>
    Structural navigation has three modes: off, document mode, and GUI mode. In document mode,
    structural navigation searches the current document or web page. In GUI (graphical user
    interface) mode, it searches the current window excluding document objects. To switch
    between these modes, use <keyseq>
      <key>Orca Modifier</key>
      <key>Z</key>
    </keyseq>.
  </p>
  <p>
    When browse mode is active, you can use structural navigation commands to move among
    interactive widgets and other document elements. If focus mode is active, switch to browse
    mode before using structural navigation commands in document content. You can configure
    whether structural navigation automatically switches Orca to focus mode when it lands on an
    interactive widget in Documents preferences.
  </p>
  <section id="settings-structural-navigation">
    <title>Settings</title>
    <p>
      <em style="strong">Preferences location:</em>
      <gui>Documents</gui> category, <gui>Structural navigation</gui> group.
    </p>
    <p>
      <em style="strong">Available settings:</em>
    </p>
    <list>
      <item>
        <p>
          <gui>Structural navigation</gui>: Controls whether
          Orca's structural navigation commands are available. Default: on.
        </p>
      </item>
      <item>
        <p>
          <gui>Automatic focus mode</gui>: Controls whether
          Orca switches to focus mode when structural navigation lands on an interactive widget.
          Default: off.
        </p>
      </item>
      <item>
        <p>
          <gui>Wrap around</gui>: Controls whether
          structural navigation wraps to the other end of the document. Default: on.
        </p>
      </item>
      <item>
        <p>
          <gui>Large object length</gui>: Sets the minimum
          number of characters for an element to be included by large object navigation
          commands. Default: 75. Range: 1 to 500.
        </p>
      </item>
      <item>
        <p>
          <gui>Skip unlabeled images</gui>: Controls whether
          image navigation skips images without accessible names or descriptions. Default: off.
        </p>
      </item>
    </list>
  </section>
